# Project context — merchant customer app (Android)

## Map
- `core/` shared library: `api/DurpallaApi.kt` (API client), `config/MerchantConfig.kt` (tenant config), `model/`, `data/AccountRepository.kt`, `auth/`, `account/`, `booking/` (Fare, Seats), `payment/`, `theme/Theme.kt`, `ui/Components.kt`.
- `app/` with product flavors **bus** (`app/src/bus/…/bus/`) and **hotel** (`app/src/hotel/…/hotel/`); each has `Flavor.kt`, `*Feature.kt`, `*Screens.kt`, `*ViewModel.kt`, mock data in `BusData.kt` / `HotelData.kt`.
- Entry: `app/src/main/…/MainActivity.kt`, `VerticalFeature.kt` (flavor plug-in point).
- Config: `settings.gradle.kts`, `app/build.gradle.kts`, `core/build.gradle.kts`, `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.
- Tests: `app/src/test` (RulesTest), screenshots in `testBus` / `testHotel` (Roborazzi).

## Commands
- Build: `./gradlew :app:assembleBusDebug` / `:app:assembleHotelDebug`
- Test: `./gradlew :app:testBusDebugUnitTest --tests "*RulesTest"` (targeted)
- Screenshots: `./gradlew :app:recordRoborazziBusDebug` (only when UI changes)

## Conventions
- Brand: bus blue `#0B3D91`, hotel teal `#0E6B63` (see `core/theme/Theme.kt`); use `PrimaryButton` etc. from `core/ui`.
- Strings Bangla + English; Bangla digits for display, ASCII for the API.
- Shared logic goes in `:core`; flavor-specific UI stays in its flavor source set.
